  "body": "`TestPackagedByDpkg` (internal/update, added in 0ac26fb52) fails on Windows at origin/main f811bf291, alone too:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestPackagedByDpkg (0.01s)\n    packaged_test.go:83: <nil>\nFAIL\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/update\n```\n\nRun: `win-run go test -count=1 -run TestPackagedByDpkg ./internal/update/` on xiaomi-gpu (Windows 11). Windows CI only compiles tests, so nothing shows it.\n\nLikely cause (not confirmed by a fix): the fixture writes `var/lib/dpkg/info/magpie:amd64.list`. On NTFS a `:` in a name makes an alternate data stream (`amd64.list` on a file named `magpie`), so the directory never lists `magpie:amd64.list` and `packagedIn` finds nothing. The code under test reads a Linux dpkg database (`goos == \"linux\"` passed in), so the fixture needs a name that can exist on Windows, or the test skips on Windows with that reason.\n\nFound while running the update package on Windows for the mycf_711 self-update fix; not touched there (one commit, one goal).\n",
