   "body": "A test-only fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4603-dpkg-fixture-windows-name), commit [5d99f4477](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/5d99f447736783b6c55d5b958be2c753dfd89033), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\n`TestPackagedByDpkg` uses a portable `magpie.list` fixture, keeping every existing assertion. The multiarch `magpie:amd64.list` suffix parsing moves to its own test, which skips on Windows because Windows reserves `:` in file names (per [Microsoft's naming rules](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/naming-a-file)); production code is unchanged.\n\nParent related packaging tests pass under `-race`; the update package vets for Windows as well. An evidence-only overlay that removes the suffix handling fails the multiarch test. The Windows binary was cross-compiled only, not executed, and no real Windows run or full suite is claimed. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
